"Some sort of time synchronization facility on your system (like <xref "
"linkend=\"ntp\"/>) is required since Kerberos won't authenticate if there is"
" a time difference between a kerberized client and the KDC server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:116
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of MIT Kerberos V5"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:125
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Build <application>MIT Kerberos V5</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:129
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cd src &amp;&amp;\n"
"sed -i -e '/eq 0/{N;s/12 //}' plugins/kdb/db2/libdb2/test/run.test &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"./configure --prefix=/usr            \\\n"
"            --sysconfdir=/etc        \\\n"
"            --localstatedir=/var/lib \\\n"
"            --runstatedir=/run       \\\n"
"            --with-system-et         \\\n"
"            --with-system-ss         \\\n"
"            --with-system-verto=no   \\\n"
"            --enable-dns-for-realm   \\\n"
"            --disable-rpath          &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#.  Note: on my laptop -j8 fails but -j1 passes
#.       For version 1.21, -j1 no longer needs to be specified and the
#.       time for the tests was reduced considerably.  -bdubbs
#.       But on one of my machines (4 cores) -j4 fails and -j1 passes...
#.       I guess the test suite is just too fragile. -xry111
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:144
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the build, issue: <command>make -j1 -k check</command>.  Some tests "
"may fail with the latest version of dejagnu and glibc.  Some tests may hang "
"for a long time and fail if the system is not connected to a network. One "
"test, <filename>t_kadm5srv</filename>, is known to fail. If <xref "
"linkend='keyutils'/> is installed but <xref linkend='keyutils-test-kernel'/>"
" is not satisfied, some tests will fail complaining <computeroutput>keyctl "
"failed with code 1</computeroutput>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:161
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:164
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>make install &amp;&amp;\n"
"cp -vfr ../doc -T /usr/share/doc/krb5-&mitkrb-version;</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:170
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:174
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <command>sed</command> command removes a test that is known to fail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:179
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--localstatedir=/var/lib</parameter>: This option is used so that"
" the Kerberos variable runtime data is located in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/var/lib</filename> instead of <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/var</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:186
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--runstatedir=/run</parameter>: This option is used so that the "
"Kerberos runtime state information is located in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/run</filename> instead of the deprecated <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/var/run</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:193
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--with-system-et</parameter>: This switch causes the build to use"
" the system-installed versions of the error-table support software."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:199
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--with-system-ss</parameter>: This switch causes the build to use"
" the system-installed versions of the subsystem command-line interface "
"software."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:205
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--with-system-verto=no</parameter>: This switch fixes a bug in "
"the package where the build system does not recognize its own verto library "
"if this package has been installed before. This is not a problem if you are "
"reinstalling the same version, but can be problematic if you are updating "
"because the old version of the verto library will be used instead of "
"installing the newer version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:214
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--enable-dns-for-realm</parameter>: This switch allows realms to "
"be resolved using the DNS server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:221
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--disable-rpath</parameter>: This switch prevents hard coding "
"library search paths (rpath) into the binary executable files and shared "
"libraries.  This package does not need rpath for an installation into the "
"standard location, and rpath may sometimes cause unwanted effects or even "
"security issues."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:229
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-ldap</option>: Use this switch if you want to compile the "
"<application>OpenLDAP</application> database backend module."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:236
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring MIT Kerberos V5"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:239
#, xml-text
msgid "Config Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:242
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<filename>/etc/krb5.conf</filename> and "
"<filename>/var/lib/krb5kdc/kdc.conf</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:247
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/krb5.conf"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:251
#, xml-text
msgid "/var/lib/krb5kdc/kdc.conf"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:257
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:260
#, xml-text
msgid "Kerberos Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><tip><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:264
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You should consider installing some sort of password checking dictionary so "
"that you can configure the installation to only accept strong passwords. A "
"suitable dictionary to use is installed in the <xref linkend=\"cracklib\"/> "
"instructions. Note that only one file can be used, but you can concatenate "
"many files into one. The configuration file shown below assumes you have "
"installed a dictionary to <filename>/usr/share/dict/words</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:275
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Create the Kerberos configuration file with the following commands issued by"
" the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:279
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/krb5.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/krb5.conf\n"
"\n"
"[libdefaults]\n"
"    default_realm = <replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"    encrypt = true\n"
"\n"
"[realms]\n"
"    <replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable> = {\n"
"        kdc = <replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"        admin_server = <replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"        dict_file = /usr/share/dict/words\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"[domain_realm]\n"
"    .<replaceable>&lt;example.org&gt;</replaceable> = <replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"\n"
"[logging]\n"
"    kdc = SYSLOG:INFO:AUTH\n"
"    admin_server = SYSLOG:INFO:AUTH\n"
"    default = SYSLOG:DEBUG:DAEMON\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/krb5.conf</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:305
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You will need to substitute your domain and proper hostname for the "
"occurrences of the <replaceable>&lt;belgarath&gt;</replaceable> and "
"<replaceable>&lt;example.org&gt;</replaceable> names."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:311
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>default_realm</option> should be the name of your domain changed to "
"ALL CAPS. This isn't required, but both <application>Heimdal</application> "
"and MIT recommend it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:317
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>encrypt = true</option> provides encryption of all traffic between "
"kerberized clients and servers. It's not necessary and can be left off. If "
"you leave it off, you can encrypt all traffic from the client to the server "
"using a switch on the client program instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:325
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <option>[realms]</option> parameters tell the client programs where to "
"look for the KDC authentication services."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:330
#, xml-text
msgid "The <option>[domain_realm]</option> section maps a domain to a realm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:334
#, xml-text
msgid "Next, create the KDC database:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:337
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>kdb5_util create -r "
"<replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable> -s</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:340
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now, you should populate the database with principals (users). For now, just"
" use your regular login name or &root;."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:344
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>kadmin.local\n"
"<prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> add_policy dict-only\n"
"<prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> addprinc -policy dict-only <replaceable>&lt;loginname&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:349
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The KDC server and any machine running kerberized server daemons must have a"
" host key installed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:353
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput><prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> addprinc -randkey "
"host/<replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:356
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"After choosing the defaults when prompted, you will have to export the data "
"to a keytab file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:360
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput><prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> ktadd "
"host/<replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:363
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This should have created a file in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc</filename> named <filename>krb5.keytab</filename> "
"(Kerberos 5). This file should have 600 (<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> rw only)  permissions. Keeping the "
"keytab files from public access is crucial to the overall security of the "
"Kerberos installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:372
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Exit the <command>kadmin</command> program (use <command>quit</command> or "
"<command>exit</command>) and return back to the shell prompt. Start the KDC "
"daemon manually, just to test out the installation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:378
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>/usr/sbin/krb5kdc</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:381
#, xml-text
msgid "Attempt to get a ticket with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:384
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>kinit <replaceable>&lt;loginname&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:387
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You will be prompted for the password you created. After you get your "
"ticket, you can list it with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:391
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>klist</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:394
#, xml-text
msgid "Information about the ticket should be displayed on the screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:399
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the functionality of the keytab file, issue the following command as"
" the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:404
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ktutil\n"
"<prompt>ktutil:</prompt> rkt /etc/krb5.keytab\n"
"<prompt>ktutil:</prompt> l</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:409
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This should dump a list of the host principal, along with the encryption "
"methods used to access the principal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:414
#, xml-text
msgid "Create an empty ACL file that can be modified later:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:417
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>touch /var/lib/krb5kdc/kadm5.acl</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:420
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"At this point, if everything has been successful so far, you can feel fairly"
" confident in the installation and configuration of the package."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:428
#, xml-text
msgid "Additional Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:431
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For additional information consult the <ulink "
"url=\"https://web.mit.edu/kerberos/www/krb5-&mitkrb-major-"
"version;/#documentation\"> documentation for krb5-&mitkrb-version;</ulink> "
"on which the above instructions are based."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:442
